{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_30","type":"agent_message","text":"A faster formulation is now clear: one scaled GEMM computes all relative projections with the reference’s required BF16 rounding, followed by a lean flash-attention kernel that gathers the needed diagonals. Local tuning selects smaller tiles for low-parallelism and short-tail cases, and larger tiles for throughput-heavy cases. I’m switching the entry point to this path and validating its numerics before the next official run."}}
